    "notes": "The 2016 grove-side photo shows the roofed entrance to the sacred path past the arch’s forked pier. A geotagged photo shows the same shelter, with a swept bamboo eave, recessed plaster opening and adjoining scalloped wall, near survey point 32. The tagged camera is southwest of the arch, on the outer side beside the fork. The model faces about 211° true across the nearby PMTiles branch. The 2 m shift east of the survey point clears both mapped roads. The exact crossing and bearing are estimated. All four viewer levels meet native terrain at three support probes. The wing has about 49 cm of embedment at its support probe. Geometry clears both PMTiles road carriageways by at least 95 cm in the tested height band, and the open passage stays clear at walking height."
  },
